    "updated_at": "2023-05-25T19:21:18Z",
    "body": "No problem. What I suggested to you in the comment above is a move away from metadata in favor of a link type.\r\n\r\nYou [can](//html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage#other-metadata-names), of course, write a specification and send it to [MetaExtensions](//wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/MetaExtensions), but this is a chore and “However, a new metadata name should not be created in any of the following cases: If the name is for something expected to have processing requirements in user agents; in that case it ought to be standardized” might be applicable given that crawlers are also UA in some way. So `<link href = .  rel = training/>` might be a good option...",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
